            <profile id="28f3-0d52-7517-9352" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="dab5-785d-be28-f228" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Hand weapon, heavy armour, and shield. May have a double-handed weapon (+4 pts) if dismounted. May have a thrusting spear (+4 pts) or lance (+4 pts), and must have a horse (free) or warhorse (+4 pts) if mounted. May take half (+4 pts) or lamellar (plate) barding (+6 pts). May have a bow (+4 pts). May take partial or full plate armour (free if mounted; partial plate is +4 pts if dismounted; full plate is +6 pts if dismounted), but may not then have a bow. Army General. Eastern Shock Cavalry if mounted and armed with a thrusting spear. 0-1 General (Basileus or Despot/Senior General). This category serves not only for those generals born to the purple (Emperors, Despots, and Caesars) but also any of the Byzantine high commanders such as Megas Domestikos, Sebastokrator, Megas Dux, or Protostrator. (Vlad the Impaler p.87)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="2ed1-52e6-4fa7-ead6" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">4+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
