            <profile id="71ce-060f-1655-dacf" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="dab5-785d-be28-f228" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Hand weapon, full plate armour, and shield. May be mounted on a horse (free) or a warhorse (+4 pts), which may have plate barding (+6 pts). If on foot, may have halberd or double-handed weapon (+4 pts). Army General. If taken, Konstantinos XI may serve as the Army General. Leader of the True Faith: any one non-allied or mercenary unit automatically passes one Panic test per game. Embodiment of the State: if Konstantinos is slain, each unit in the Byzantine army and all allied and mercenary units take the resultant Panic test at -1 to their Leadership. Paleologan Byzantines only. (Vlad the Impaler p.90)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="a0dd-11ea-b50f-f25e" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">3+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <!-- armour-save -->
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <infoLinks>
