  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="9d72-2e51-5e13-5bf1" name="Byzantine Empire (Vlad the Impaler) - List Notes" publicationId="dab5-785d-be28-f228" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF BYZANTIUM (Vlad the Impaler, pp.86-90): the Paleologan Byzantines (1280-1453), the Despotates of Epiros and Thessaly and the Despotate of the Morea. Allies from other lists are documented only.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Byzantine Empire - Paleologan Byzantines (1280-1453)]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 25%
  Infantry: up to 25%
  Allies and Mercenaries: up to 75%
  PALEOLOGAN BYZANTINES, 1280-1453. Characters up to 25% (may take a Basileus as Army General); Cavalry up to 25%; Infantry up to 25% (may only take 0-1 Mangonel or artillery piece for each 1,000 pts; Bombards may only be taken after 1420); Allies and Mercenaries up to 75%. Additionally, Paleologan armies may take allies from Serbians (1327-1352; any Serbian troops, Vlastella limited to 0-1 per 1,000 pts), Bulgarians (1327-1352; any Bulgarian troops, Pronija Retainers limited to 0-1 per 1,000 pts, no Provincial Pronija), Ottomans (1327-1442; any Ottoman infantry or cavalry, Sipahi limited to 0-1 per 1,000 pts, no Kapikulu) and Italian Condotta from Armies of Chivalry (any Italian cavalry or infantry, Mercenary Knights limited to 0-1 per 1,000 pts, no Feudal Knights) - documented only.
[Byzantine Empire - Despotates of Epiros (1280-1340) and Thessaly (1280-1318)]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 25%
  Infantry: up to 25%
  Allies and Mercenaries: up to 75%
  DESPOTATES OF EPIROS, 1280-1340; THESSALY, 1280-1318. Characters up to 25% (may not take a Basileus); Cavalry up to 25% (Pronoia/Stratiotai only; no other cavalry choices); Infantry up to 25% (may not take Tzakones Militia; may only take 0-1 Mangonel for each 1,000 pts; Bombards may not be taken); Allies and Mercenaries up to 75% (Latinikoi Knights and Skythikoi, which must be Vlachs; allies from Paleologan Byzantines (1309-1310: Pronoia/Stratiotai and 0-1 Kavallarioi), Albanian allies (1280-1340: only Epirotes, Stradioti, Harketar and Qites) and Bulgar allies (1280-1318: only Bulgar Horse Archers and Ichirgu, only by Thessaly) are documented only).
[Byzantine Empire - Despotate of the Morea (1280-1460)]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 25%
  Infantry: up to 25%
  Allies and Mercenaries: up to 75%
  DESPOTATE OF THE MOREA, 1280-1460. Characters up to 25% (may not take a Basileus); Cavalry up to 25% (Pronoia/Stratiotai only; no other cavalry choice is available); Infantry up to 25% (may not take Tzakones Militia; may only take 0-1 Mangonel or artillery piece for each 1,000 pts; Bombards may only be taken after 1420); Allies and Mercenaries up to 75% (Maniates/Melingioi, Latinikoi Knights (1459-1460) and 0-1 Italian Men-at-Arms (1459-1460); allies from Paleologan Byzantines (1280-1347: Kavallarioi, Kontaritoi and Pronoia/Stratiotai only), Albanian (from 1347: Stradioti, Harketar and Qites only), Hungarian (1445-1450: Crusader Knights and Sergeants only) and Ottoman (1382-1394: Akinci, Azab/Yaya and Voynuks) are documented only).</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
